<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9a349771-f3a3-5f81-ab18-85a4a747f92a" activityNameId="88e51724-a049-56a7-b61e-9027d2113c82" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Operation, freight train</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Operation, freight train
Average data for the operation of goods transportation by rail in Belgium. The data has been determined top down, by combining the total yearly energy consumption and the yearly tkm-performance of goods transportation.;
UUID: d35989a0-8bb5-3262-ae17-555a59bc4350
The inventory includes the actual energy consumption for an average goods train (1289Gt) in Belgium using electro and diesel energy. In addition the diesel consumption and emissions of shunting processes are accounted for.
Location: Data refers to average goods transport conditions in Belgium, some extrapolation from switzerland has been made: diesel consumption for shunting, particle matters from abrasion processes
Technology: diesel and electric traction, diesel traction for shunting
Time period: Data for emission indices for shunting  is based on figures of 1995, specific energy consumption per tkm is from 2011
Production volume: 9357 Mio. tkm in 2007  in Belgium
Sampling: International  Railway statistic 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d35989a0-8bb5-3262-ae17-555a59bc4350.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f5f722ed-cace-5738-bbab-d3554c24a58a" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
